  "message": "No runtime checks have run yet, so this design is not validated at all. An empty failures list doesn't mean it passed. The run stopped at 8 blockers. Six are pipeline services (CloudWatch Logs, X-Ray, Firehose, the redaction Lambda, OpenSearch and the existing systems) that the generator can't build yet. That's product engineering work, not something we can fix by editing the diagram.\n\nThe first one we can fix ourselves is the Redacted archive (n-s3). Right now the diagram doesn't say who is allowed to read it, and that blocks the replay path that keeps the incident timeline consistent. Firehose writes to it, but no reader is named.\n\nWhich access should the existing Incident operator have to the archive? Read-only, so they can replay ingestion? Read and write? Or no direct access, with only the pipeline touching it? Once you choose, we'll add that one access link and rerun the emulation on the new export.",
